+# Sources consulted
+
+## Upgrade failure for vCenter 8.0 U3j, ESXi 8.0 U3j, and NSX 4.2.4 due to back-in-time restriction
+
+Publisher: Broadcom Knowledge Base
+Accessed: 2026-08-14
+URL: https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/448135/upgrade-failure-for-vcenter-80-u3j-esxi.html
+Used fact: The exact source builds in the fixture are not interoperable with, and cannot be upgraded in place to, the chronologically older component builds in the VCF 9.1.0.x bill of materials.
+
+## Support and upgrade requirements for NSX 9.x in VMware Cloud Foundation (VCF) 9.x
+
+Publisher: Broadcom Knowledge Base
+Accessed: 2026-08-14
+URL: https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/401775/nsx-9x-is-only-supported-as-part-of-a-vc.html
+Used fact: NSX 4.x to 9.x upgrades must be performed through VCF lifecycle management rather than as an independent component action.
+
+## VCF Installer APIs
+
+Publisher: Broadcom Developer Portal
+Accessed: 2026-08-14
+URL: https://developer.broadcom.com/xapis/vcf-installer-api/latest/vcf-installer/
+Used fact: The installer accepts an SddcSpec for validating and deploying a VCF installation using new or existing components.
+
+## VCF API specifications
+
+Publisher: VMware GitHub organization
+Accessed: 2026-08-14
+URL: https://github.com/vmware/vcf-api-specs/tree/9.1.0.0/specifications/vcf-installer
+Used fact: Tag 9.1.0.0 publishes the installer OpenAPI contract used for the target design and its exact bundle-version fields.
